  "user_request_original": "Design a 36-layer custom dielectric filter on fused silica substrate with air incidence at 0 degrees, unpolarized light. Stack structure: Air | alternating Ta2O5 (Gao) and SiO2 (Gao) layers (36 total layers, 18 of each material) | Fused Silica. Initialize layer thicknesses with mixed pattern: layers 1-18 near 355 nm quarter-wave condition, layers 19-36 near 1050 nm quarter-wave condition. Optimize all 36 individual layer thicknesses within 20-350 nm bounds to balance minimization of average transmittance in 355-365 nm and 1030-1080 nm bands while maintaining high average transmittance in 420-700 nm band. Report final layer thickness sequence and transmittance spectra across 350-1100 nm.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Design a 36-layer Ta2O5/SiO2 dielectric filter on fused silica at 0 degrees unpolarized incidence. Initialize alternating layers with mixed quarter-wave thicknesses near 355 nm and 1050 nm. Optimize all 36 thicknesses within 20-350 nm to minimize average transmittance in 355-365 nm and 1030-1080 nm bands while maximizing it in 420-700 nm.",
